      "defect": "IAM role-to-user ratio exceeds 200:1.\n",
      "infection": "Each IAM role is a potential credential source via sts:AssumeRole. At extreme ratios, role governance becomes impractical: unused roles accumulate, trust policies go unreviewed, and the blast radius of a single trust policy misconfiguration expands. Service-linked roles created automatically by AWS services add to the count even when the service is no longer used.\n",
      "failure": "Non-human identity sprawl without governance. Unused roles persist as dormant credential sources, increasing the attack surface for lateral movement and privilege escalation.\n",
